      "reasoning": "I checked the hand and then kept the second deal.\n\nWhat I did (actions taken)\n- Called get_action_choices to view the mulligan offer and hand.\n- Mulliganed the first 7 (hand looked mana-screwed/awkward).\n- Called get_action_choices again on the redraw and chose to keep that hand.\n\nHands (quick summary)\n- First hand (mulliganed): 1 land (Inventors' Fair), several heavy-blue spells (Whir of Invention, Ponder, Negate) and only one land — too risky.\n- Second hand (kept): Buried Ruin (land), Sol Ring, Fiery Gambit, Temur Battle Rage, Long-Term Plans, Tribute Mage, The Locust God.\n\nReasoning (short, analytical)\n- The redraw had Sol Ring + Buried Ruin — immediate ramp/recur synergy — and a high-value top-end (Locust God). That card quality is attractive in a free mulligan decision.\n- Big caveat: the kept hand currently has no blue or red mana sources (Buried Ruin and Sol Ring produce colorless), so many cards in hand are uncastable until we draw colored mana. This is a real risk and would normally push toward another mulligan, but the combination of Sol Ring + Buried Ruin + Locust God made keeping defensible in expectation of drawing a colored land soon.\n- I prioritized preserving the explosive potential and artifact synergy over the lower-probability of finding colored mana after another mulligan.\n\nPlanned next steps\n- Turn 1 play: drop Buried Ruin and cast Sol Ring (use Sol Ring to accelerate future turns and increase the chance to cast colored spells once a colored land is drawn).\n- From there, look to draw a colored source on turn 2 or 3; if not, pivot to artifact recursion/interaction lines and try to assemble a playable line (Buried Ruin can recur artifacts later).\n\nIf you want, I can continue into turn 1 and execute the play (pass_priority -> get_action_choices -> choose_action) now.",
