      "reasoning": "I control a tapped Forest (p2) and have three lands left in hand: Boros Guildgate, Plains, and Mountain. It's my second turn, and I haven't played a land yet this turn (land_drops_used: 0), so I can play one.\n\nTo enable casting two-mana green spells like *Elvish Rejuvenator* or *Far Wanderings* this turn, I need another green source. I already have a Forest in play, so adding a Mountain or Boros Guildgate won't help with green.\n\nHowever, I also need to develop mana to cast *Waker of the Wilds* ({2}{G}{G}) and *Emeria Shepherd* ({5}{W}{W}), so color balance matters.\n\nBest option: Play the **Plains** (p3).  \nWhy?  \n- I already have green from Forest.  \n- I need white for *Emeria Shepherd* and potential lifegain synergy.  \n- Boros Guildgate produces red and white but enters tapped — I’ll save it for when I need the color fixing and can afford the tempo.  \n- Mountain gives red, which *Waker of the Wilds* needs, but I can’t cast it yet anyway without more lands.  \n\nPlaying the Plains sets up future double-white costs and keeps my tapland for later smoothing.\n\nI’ll play Plains now.\n\n\n\n",
