      "player": "Qwen3L Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "It's the **end step** of my turn, and I have priority.\n\nI have 4 untapped lands:\n- Forest (p2)\n- Plains (p3)\n- Mountain (p4)\n- Forest (p20, which just entered tapped — but all lands untap during the untap step, which is next turn, so it remains tapped).\n\nWait — p20 is tapped, so **untapped_lands: 3**?\n\nBut get_action_choices says `untapped_lands: 4` — that means p20 is untapped? Or perhaps the game tracks differently.\n\nAnyway, I have enough mana to cast spells.\n\nI can cast **Harrow** ({2}{G}) — I have plenty of green and generic mana.\n\nIs it worth casting in the end step?\n\nHarrow is a sorcery — I **cannot** cast it during my end step.\n\nBut here it's listed under \"Play instants and activated abilities\" — and Harrow is a sorcery.\n\nThat should not be playable.\n\nYet `get_action_choices` lists it in `choices` with `\"action\":\"cast\"` — that suggests it is being allowed.\n\nBut that violates game rules.\n\nUnless… did I misremember? Is Harrow an instant?\n\nNo — Harrow is a sorcery.\n\nLet me confirm.\n\nCall get_oracle_text for Harrow (p12).\n\n\n\n\n",
