      "player": "Qwen3L Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Harrow's rules:\n> As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a land.  \n> Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\n\nThis is not the Harrow I know. This must be a different card with the same name — or a variant.\n\nWait — standard Harrow is {1}{G}, sorcery, \"Exile target land. Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. Suspend 2— (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {1}{G} and exile it with two time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, cast it without paying its mana cost.)\"\n\nThis is not matching.\n\nThe oracle text says: \"As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a land.\" — that sounds like a different card.\n\nPerhaps this is a custom or alternate version.\n\nBut the mana cost is {2}{G} — same as before.\n\nAnd it's in my hand as Harrow (p12).\n\nBut important: if it has \"sacrifice a land\" as an additional cost, then casting it requires sacrificing one of my lands.\n\nI currently have 4 lands — sacrificing one would leave me with 3.\n\nAnd I'm being offered to cast it during my end step — which suggests it's a sorcery? But sorceries can't be cast then.\n\nUnless this version is an instant.\n\nThe oracle text doesn't specify type.\n\nBut in the `get_action_choices` list, it's presented as castable in the end step — which only allows instants and activated abilities.\n\nTherefore, this **Harrow** must be an **instant**.\n\nOtherwise, it wouldn't be in the list.\n\nSo despite the name, it's likely an instant with flash.\n\nSo I can cast it now.\n\nBut should I?\n\nCost: {2}{G} + sacrifice a land.\n\nEffect: search for up to two basic lands, put them onto the battlefield.\n\nThis is similar to Kodama's Reach, but with \"sacrifice a land\" as cost.\n\nI already played Kodama's Reach this turn — casting this now would net me **one additional basic land** (since I lose one, gain up to two).\n\nBut I just got to 4 lands — sacrificing one would hurt my tempo.\n\nAnd I just fetched with Kodama’s — better to hold this for later, when I need a surprise land drop or to recover from land destruction.\n\nAlso, casting it now lets opponents see my new lands — they may counter with graveyard hate or land destruction.\n\nBest to **save it** for a more opportune time.\n\nI will **not** cast it now.\n\nI pass priority.\n\nFinal decision: **do nothing**, end my turn.\n\n\n\n",
