      "player": "Qwen3L Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I made a mistake — I passed to \"my_turn\", but now I’m in combat of my previous turn? That doesn’t make sense.\n\nLooking back: after I discarded, I should have moved to the next player.\n\nBut the context now says: \"T2 Combat/Declare Attackers (Qwen3L Libby)\" — so it's still turn 2, my combat phase.\n\nI completely missed combat earlier.\n\nDuring my turn, after casting Kodama’s Reach, I passed directly to end step — but I should have had the option to attack.\n\nThat’s a major oversight.\n\nIn multiplayer Magic, every turn has a combat phase where you can attack.\n\nI should have attacked with a creature — but I didn’t play any creatures this turn.\n\nI cast Kodama’s Reach — an enchantment — and lands.\n\nNo creatures in play.\n\nTherefore, I have no attackers.\n\nSo I should pass combat.\n\nBut now the game is asking me to cast spells during combat — which is fine, but I have nothing useful to do.\n\nThe only spell available is Harrow (instant version), which requires sacrificing a land — not worth it during combat.\n\nI should pass.\n\nBut the phase is \"Declare Attackers\" — and I have no creatures.\n\nI must declare attackers — either by declaring one or passing.\n\nSince I have no creatures, I should pass.\n\nBut `get_action_choices` shows \"Play instants and activated abilities\", not \"declare attackers\".\n\nThat means I’m in the **beginning of combat** step, not declare attackers yet.\n\nI can cast instants.\n\nBut with no creatures, attacking is pointless.\n\nBest to pass priority to move to declare attackers.\n\nThen, when that prompt comes, I can skip.\n\nBut since I have no creatures, I should let combat pass.\n\nI’ll pass priority now.\n\ncall_choose_action(answer=false)\n\n\n\n\n",
