      "ts": "2026-02-15T12:14:36.155-08:00",
      "player": "Qwen3L Libby",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Now I'm in my **postcombat main phase**.\n\nI have 4 untapped lands: {G}{G}{W}{R} available.\n\nI can play a land — I have Plains (p28) in hand.\n\nAnd I can cast:\n\n- Waker of the Wilds ({2}{G}{G}) — cost 4, I have enough\n- Elvish Rejuvenator ({2}{G}) — 3-mana 1/1 with lifelink and landfall\n- Harrow ({2}{G}) — instant with \"sacrifice a land\" cost — not ideal now\n- Far Wanderings ({2}{G}) — enchantment\n\nBest play: **Waker of the Wilds** — a 3/3 with trample, and whenever a land enters, I get a 3/3 Elemental token.\n\nI already have multiple lands entering (from ramp), so it will trigger immediately.\n\nI also have one land in hand: the Plains fetched from Kodama's Reach.\n\nI should play the Plains first, then cast Waker.\n\nWhy?\n\n- If I cast Waker first, then play Plains — the landfall trigger from Waker will create a token immediately.\n- If I play Plains first, tap it for mana? But I already have enough — no need.\n\nBut Waker’s ability triggers whenever a land enters the battlefield — even if not tapped for mana.\n\nSo if I play the Plains first, that triggers Waker — but Waker isn’t in play yet — no trigger.\n\nI must cast Waker **after** playing the land, so that it sees the land enter.\n\nSequence:\n1. Play Plains (p28) — now 5 lands in play, one tapped (the one from Reach), others untapped.\n2. Cast Waker of the Wilds ({2}{G}{G}) — cost 4: {G}{G}{2}\n   - Tap two Forests for {G}{G}\n   - Tap Plains and Mountain for {1}{1}\n   - Total: {G}{G}{2} → pay cost\n3. When Waker enters, it doesn’t trigger from the Plains — because the Plains entered earlier.\n4. But I can let other lands trigger it later.\n\nI have no way to make the Plains trigger Waker, unless I flicker or re-enter a land.\n\nSo better to:\n\n1. Cast Waker of the Wilds first — with current 4 lands\n2. Then play the Plains — that will trigger Waker, creating a 3/3 Elemental token with trample.\n\nYes — much better.\n\nSo:\n- Tap three lands: two Forests, Mountain → {G}{