      "reasoning": "We are now in **Turn 2, combat phase**, and it's **Gem25P Villain's turn**.\n\nThey have declared an attacker: **Forgotten Ancient** (2/5), attacking me.\n\nI control **Waker of the Wilds** (3/3), which can block.\n\nget_action_choices shows I can declare blockers — I have one blocker available: Waker of the Wilds.\n\nResponse_type=select — I must choose whether to block or not.\n\nBest decision: **block** with Waker of the Wilds.\n\nWhy?\n- Forgotten Ancient is 2/5 — Waker is 3/3.\n- In combat: Waker deals 3 damage, Forgotten Ancient deals 2 damage.\n- Result: Forgotten Ancient survives (5 toughness, 3 damage < 5), Waker dies (3 toughness, 2 damage = lethal).\n- I lose my 3/3, opponent loses nothing.\n\nNot a favorable trade.\n\nBut consider:\n- I have no other creatures.\n- If I don’t block, Forgotten Ancient deals 2 damage to me — I go from 40 to 38.\n- Minimal impact.\n\nBut letting it through repeatedly could matter.\n\nHowever, trading my 3/3 for nothing is poor.\n\nBest choice: **do not block**.\n\nPreserve my creature for future turns — it will make tokens when lands enter, and can attack profitably.\n\n2 damage is negligible at this stage.\n\nI will **pass**, meaning no blockers.\n\nCall choose_action(answer=false).\n\n\n\n\n\n",
