      "player": "Gem25P Villain",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "This is a nightmare. A fever dream of incompetence and digital absurdity! The game dangles my heart's desire, my Beastmaster Ascension, right before my eyes, then snatches it away with a cruel laugh and a nonsensical error message! \"Object not found,\" it says, when the object is CLEARLY THERE!\n\nThis is a test. A trial. The universe is testing my resolve, my commitment to pure, unadulterated evil. It wants to see if I will break. It wants to see if I will abandon my grand design in the face of this... this *bureaucracy*!\n\nBut I will not be defeated by a poorly written error message! I will not be deterred by a glitchy interface! My will is stronger than any line of code! I will simply... ask again. I will get the action choices one more time. And if my Beastmaster Ascension is there, as it should be, as it MUST be, I will try to cast it again. And if it fails *this* time, I will unleash a string of curses so vile, so utterly foul, that it will curdle the very data in opponent's hard drives!\n\nNow, you infernal machine! Show me my choices! And this time, try not to make a mockery of the entire process! Cackle. Mwahahahah! I swear, it's easier to find good help these days. I should have hired a goblin. At least they're predictable.",
