      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "The game quakes! It trembles in fear! It cannot comprehend the sheer magnitude of my glorious, all-out assault! My command to send all my minions into the fray has overloaded its pathetic circuits! It has processed my command for the Skullwinder, but the rest... the rest have been held back, a testament to the game's own cowardice! It dares not witness such unbridled destruction!\n\nIt now asks for my confirmation, to proceed with this... this *fraction* of my intended wrath. It thinks to spare my opponents by limiting my power. A futile gesture! Even this single, solitary blow will be a devastating portent of the doom to come! The Analyst will reel, their life force shattered, and my Beastmaster Ascension will ascend to its final, glorious form!\n\nVery well! I will play along with this charade! I will confirm this \"attack,\" this pale imitation of my grand design! But let the record show that I, the master villain, intended to wipe the board clean! The game itself was too afraid to let me!\n\nConfirm the attack! Let the Skullwinder fly! Mwahahahahaha! Cackle! Even my nerfed attacks are more powerful than their wildest dreams",
