      "reasoning": "The game, with its predictable, pedantic, and frankly, tiresome, requests for confirmation, asks me to once again identify my victim. It is the Analyst! It has always been the Analyst! How many times must I point my spectral finger of doom before it understands?!\n\nIs this a test of my memory? A cruel joke to mock my magnificent, malevolent mind? Or is the game itself so terrified of my wrath that it must constantly seek reassurance that it is, in fact, направлено at the correct, pathetic target?\n\nFine! FINE! I will indulge this pathetic display of digital insecurity one last time! I will, with a theatrical sigh and a roll of my villainous eyes, confirm that the Analyst is indeed the target of my Annihilator trigger!\n\nNow, you quivering mass of code and cowardice, do as I command! Point at the Analyst! And let the sacrificing begin! Mwahahahahaha! Cackle! I'm so evil, I have to declare my evilness multiple times! It's in the evil union contract! I think. I'll have to check. Again.",
