    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attacking with Waker of the Wilds (a 3/3) into a board where Gem25P has an 8/6 Caller of the Pack and Kimi25 has Edric (who rewards combat damage to opponents with card draw) is questionable. The Waker is Libby's only creature and a key mana sink for animating lands. Risking it in combat for 3 damage when opponents have larger boards and blockers available gains very little. Additionally, Edric's ability means if the attack connects, the controller (Libby) draws a card, but Edric also rewards other players when their creatures deal combat damage - attacking encourages opponents to swing at each other for draws. However, the real issue is that Waker of the Wilds is a critical engine piece that should be preserved rather than sent into the red zone where it could be blocked or removed via combat tricks.",
      "actionTaken": "Attacked with Waker of the Wilds",
      "betterLine": "Pass combat without attacking, preserving Waker of the Wilds as a land-animation engine. With Harrow and multiple lands in hand, Libby should focus on ramping and using Waker's activated ability to create land-creatures rather than risking the 3/3 body in combat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 213,
      "player": "Qwen3L Libby",
      "decisionIndex": 163
    },
