    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Evolutionary Escalation requires putting +1/+1 counters on an opponent's creature. The three options were Ohran Viper (1/3 deathtouch + combat damage draw), Skullwinder (1/3 deathtouch), and Caller of the Pack (8/6 trample with myriad). Putting counters on Caller of the Pack makes an already-huge creature slightly bigger (11/9), but it already has trample and myriad so the marginal impact of +3/+3 is relatively small compared to buffing a smaller creature. However, Skullwinder also has deathtouch, meaning the +1/+1 counters don't meaningfully improve it as a combat threat since it already kills anything it touches. The real concern is that a 4/6 deathtouch is harder to attack into. Caller of the Pack with myriad creates token copies when attacking, and those copies would also be 11/9 with trample, making it significantly more dangerous in a multiplayer game. Putting counters on Caller of the Pack is arguably the worst choice since it amplifies myriad damage across all opponents, but Skullwinder gaining +3/+3 on a deathtouch body also makes it a more threatening blocker/attacker. This is debatable but Caller of the Pack with myriad multiplying the bonus across multiple combat instances is likely the worse target to avoid.",
